    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37805" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑή,
		ἑόν,</span> dat. written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱῷ</span> [^
		-] <i><span class="en">
			Maiist.
			10
		</span></i>; 
			Boeot.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱός</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Corinn.
			<u>Supp.</u>
			2.73
		</span></i>; possess.Adj.of <i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i> pers.sg., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>his, her own,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>, 
				Dor.
			, Thess. (<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).250
			</span></i>); not in 
				Att.
			 Prose (unless in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				350
			</span></i> the word is Plato's), dub. in Trag., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				1206
			</span></i> (lyr.):—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἑόν τε
				Πόδαργον</span>
			<i>his own</i> Podargus, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.295
			</span></i>; strengthd., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑῷ αὐτοῦ
			θυμῷ</span> in <i>his own inmost</i> soul, <i><span class="en">
				10.204
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑοὶ αὐτοῦ θῆτες</span>
			<i>his own</i> labourers, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.643
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> after <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>(also v.l.
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.393
			</span></i>, al.), of other persons, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> as Adj.
			<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i> pers. pl., <i>their,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.91
			</span></i>, freq. in later 
				Ep.
			, as <i><span class="en">
				Batr.
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1113
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i> Poets, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.226
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> also, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Batr.
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.634
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.140
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.50
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέτερος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.203
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμέτερος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.332
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.267
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.730
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pers.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				1.468
			</span></i>. (I.-<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>sewo-,</i> Lat. <i>suus;</i> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς.</span>)</div>
